{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings/settings_tabs.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:02.598804Z","id":"80bf43814acec51a85f8fd53cd4d8ffc49b000e9a2c927746c5fb27ddfb88c0a","body":{"detail":"The phone's sections (§5.5) are Claude, Dictation, Sharing, Notifications, Home screen, About and Developer; §4.5's tabs cover all but About, so About became General. Clax › About Clax (apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/AppDelegate.swift showAbout) also shows the version and a haiku, so the Mac shows them twice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":18},"content_hash":"d11933179572ec6b9f22507ad1b670b146e265e050ec263913068f8ea3335b47"},"summary":"What the General tab holds: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.5 names General (gearshape) without its contents; it holds the phone's About section (Clax's and the home screen's versions, Licences, the haiku). Is that the owner's General?","tags":["status:needs-decision","settings","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings/settings_tabs.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:43:02.598879Z","id":"9a3d5aad4d5e1cc213e7936bee33d9741001d4558795a94ef9193295f997e808","body":{"detail":"The tab reads 'Apps you allow can remind you' or 'Turn them on for the reminders apps set' (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart, SettingsTab.notifications in _form), from the native channel's notificationsAllowed (apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift). §4.5 lists it as its own tab.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"34518096bcbd90bff5adac2f0c42f0c47fea9f603b68aa88ebbe53944112faad"},"summary":"The Mac's Notifications tab says only whether notifications are on, with Open System Settings: the Mac shows no run notices (lib/main.dart gives it NoBackgroundWork), only the reminders apps set, and the Comment tab's switch is the phone's. Keep the tab, or fold it into General?","tags":["status:needs-decision","settings","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
